Item 02 is done and the gate passed. Nothing further is pending; not every item is checked, so no completion marker.

**What was built.** `learning/obstruction_expansion.py` with a C helper `learning/obstruction_expansion.c`: a tabu search per level `t` for small closed neighbourhoods (restarts from maximal cliques, the witness's prefix sets, BFS balls, and the neighbouring levels, then focus rounds on the argmax levels), an exact profile over all `2^n` subsets at `n ≤ 22`, the cap-12 branch-and-bound floor as a harness candidate, and stages `ceiling`, `exact`, `floor`, `tables`. Nine tests in `tests/test_obstruction_expansion.py`. Report §2 in `reports/obstruction_search.md`; files under `reports/scratch/obstruction_search/02_expansion/`.

**Headline finding.** On 320 of the 338 bound-gap instances the search's ceiling sits below the optimum, so Harper's expansion family cannot close them under any computation, however deep the cap. On 249 of the 338 the ceiling is at or below the best floor already on record. Only 18 remain possible for the family; the floor closes 7 and 11 go to item 03. Over all 4,697 targets the ceiling is never above the optimum, and the family's duality gap is exact (floor = ceiling) on 4,547.

**Other numbers.**
- Exact at `n ≤ 22`: the search attains the exact profile at every level on 99.2% of 4,123 instances, the ceiling equals the exact bound on all of them, and Harper exact is tight on 71% (kill criterion not met).
- Floor rerun on the 35 instances item 01 censored: up on 32, by up to 6 stacks, and above the best floor on record on 17 (the dense 125 × 125 classes).
- Harness validity run on all 6,376: above optimum 0; beats the reference `max(lb_best, tw + 1)` on 73 of the 338.
- A second search pass (seed 2, triple budget) changes the ceiling by ±1 on 4 of 436 instances.

**One correction recorded.** The item's text suggested seeding from a customer *closing* order; that layout has no vertex-separation guarantee (56 against 24 on `Random-125-125-2-2_0`). The *opening*-time layout has vertex separation exactly `optimum − 1` on every target and is what the `ceiling ≤ optimum` guarantee rests on; a test asserts it.

**Compute.** 3.4 core-hours against the item's 3 (floor 2.83, harness 0.32, ceiling 0.14, second pass 0.13); the floor's 10-minute cap was halved where only one level was missing, stated in the report.

